% ============================================================================
% precipitation-types.query.adj — a worked recall over the meteorology
% precipitation-types library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is snow made of?": it
% states no weather fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table and
% asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the `precip_form`
% rows and returns the form + the table's source/locator/trust. The fourth query
% runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the form `balls_of_ice`, recall its
% precipitation type — hail). A word that is not one of these precipitation types
% abstains honestly — the engine never invents a form.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli precipitation-types.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "precipitation-types.adj"

? precip_form(snow, $Form)            % expect ice_crystals
? precip_form(sleet, $Form)           % expect frozen_raindrops
? precip_form(freezing_rain, $Form)   % expect glaze_of_ice
? precip_form($Precip, balls_of_ice)  % reverse bind — expect hail
? precip_form(fog, $Form)             % expect abstain — fog is suspended droplets, not one of the falling precipitation types
